From e47f1143f3d9d32fad0d4c0b8c757c3e80b1b092 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Casati <diego.casati@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:44:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] LinuxKPI: 802.11 station controlled port and strict
 regulatory

- Gate the WPA2 controlled port on a TX-acked EAPOL M4, installed
  PTK/GTK with replay counters, and firmware peer authorization, using
  the new net80211 iv_port_authorize hook.
- Add opt-in strict handling of self-managed regulatory domains: the
  channel list is rebuilt from the driver's regd, and TX is revoked if
  it cannot be applied.  NO_IR, DFS and indoor channels are kept as
  passive-only rather than dropped.
- Under strict regulatory, 5 GHz channels allow HT40 in the aligned
  direction and VHT80 when one rule spans the aligned 40/80 MHz block
  and no overlapping rule has a narrower bandwidth, lower EIRP or gain,
  or a NO_IR/DFS flag the primary channel lacks.  2.4 GHz stays at
  20 MHz and 160 MHz is never enabled.
- Add the cfg80211, mac80211 and ieee80211 header pieces ath12k needs.
- cfg80211_find_vendor_ie() now returns a const pointer, as in Linux;
  adapt ath10k and ath11k.
- Per-channel regulatory exclusions are only logged with the
  D80211_CHANDEF debug flag set.

Drivers that do not opt in keep their current behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Diego Casati <diego.casati@gmail.com>
